---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Cmd from '../components/Cmd.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import { faqPick, site } from '../content/site';
import { mdInline } from '../content/readme';

const title = 'Claude Code memory between sessions | hippo';
const description =
  "Hippo adds a local store of lessons beside Claude Code's CLAUDE.md and auto memory. In our own test on 29 repositories, against built-in memory alone, repeat mistakes fell from 21 in 100 to 11 at the same cost.";

// README "Framework Integrations": what `hippo init` adds to Claude Code's settings.
const hooks = [
  { event: 'SessionStart', does: "Prints the rules you've stated and what the last sleep did." },
  { event: 'UserPromptSubmit', does: 'Keeps pinned memories and the last 5 writes in context, and adds memories that match the prompt. An unchanged block is skipped.' },
  { event: 'PreCompact', does: 'Saves a snapshot of the task before the transcript is summarised.' },
  { event: 'SessionStart (compact)', does: 'Puts that snapshot back into context after compaction.' },
  { event: 'PostCompact', does: 'Tells you what was saved.' },
  { event: 'PostToolUseFailure', does: 'Stores a failed tool call as an error memory. It skips interrupts, declined permissions and empty searches, and stores a repeated failure once.' },
  { event: 'SessionEnd', does: 'Runs `hippo sleep`, then `hippo capture` on the session transcript.' },
];

const plugin = `${site.links.repo}/tree/master/extensions/claude-code-plugin`;
---

<Base title={title} description={description} crumb="Claude Code" published="2026-09-28">
  <Nav />
  <main id="main">
    <PageIntro>
      <Fragment slot="title">Claude Code memory <span class="text-gradient">between sessions</span></Fragment>
      <p>
        Claude Code already loads your <code>CLAUDE.md</code> files and its own auto memory notes into every session.
        Hippo runs beside them and keeps what comes up as you work, such as a rule you stated, a tool call that failed or
        a fact that changed. In our test on 29 repositories, Claude Code with hippo added repeated a corrected mistake 11
        times in 100, against 21 with built-in memory alone, at the same cost. We can't yet say how much of that the
        stored lessons carry.
      </p>
    </PageIntro>

    <Section title="Set it up" id="set-it-up-in-two-commands">
      <Cmd lines={[site.installCmd, 'hippo init']} copy />
      <p>
        <code>hippo init</code> adds a short block to the project's <code>CLAUDE.md</code> if it has one, adds seven hook
        entries to <code>~/.claude/settings.json</code>, and schedules a daily run at 6:15am that stores lessons from the
        day's commits. <code>hippo init --no-hooks --no-schedule</code> skips both, and <code>hippo doctor</code> checks
        the install.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="What each hook does" id="what-the-hooks-do" alt>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-white/8" data-scroll-x>
        <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
          <caption class="sr-only">Claude Code hooks that hippo init installs</caption>
          <thead class="bg-white/[0.03] font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-400">
            <tr>
              <th scope="col" class="px-3 py-3 font-medium sm:px-5">Hook</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-3 py-3 font-medium sm:px-5">What it does</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5">
            {hooks.map((h) => (
              <tr class="align-top">
                <th scope="row" class="px-3 py-3 text-left font-mono text-xs font-normal text-accent-light sm:whitespace-nowrap sm:px-5">{h.event}</th>
                <td class="copy px-3 py-3 text-zinc-300 sm:px-5" set:html={mdInline(h.does)} />
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        The <a class="link" href={plugin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Claude Code plugin<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a>
        is the alternative to these hooks. Use one, not both.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Rules and failures are kept for you" id="a-mistakes-file-that-maintains-itself">
      <p>
        A rule you state to the agent is captured and printed back at the start of later sessions. In a replay of 16
        sessions, agents followed those rules in all 16 with the session-start hook and in none with the per-prompt hook
        alone. Capture has been wrong before. An earlier version pinned 83 rows from 27 real sessions, "Don't worry about
        it" among them, and the fix pins 6.
      </p>
      <Cmd
        lines={[
          'hippo remember "billing uses pnpm; never run npm install here" --error',
          'hippo outcome --bad',
          'hippo supersede mem_a1b2c3 "billing moved to bun"',
          'hippo failures',
        ]}
      />
      <p>These add a lesson, mark the last recall wrong, replace a fact and list what the failure hook saw.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Memories you can read and commit" alt>
      <p>
        The store is SQLite, in <code>.hippo/hippo.db</code> in each project, plus <code>~/.hippo/</code> for lessons
        shared across projects. Hippo writes markdown mirrors beside it, so you can read, grep and commit what your agent
        has been told. Codex, Cursor and any MCP client read the same store.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="MCP, and where CLAUDE.md fits">
      <p>
        <code>claude mcp add hippo-memory -- hippo mcp</code> gives Claude Code hippo's memory tools over MCP. Keep
        <code>CLAUDE.md</code> for short standing rules. The
        <a class="link" href="/vs/claude-memory/">CLAUDE.md vs memory</a> page covers what goes where, and
        <code>hippo import --claude CLAUDE.md</code> turns notes that piled up there into memories.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Faq
      items={faqPick(['How do I give Claude Code memory between sessions?'])}
      heading="Claude Code questions"
      moreHref="/faq/"
    />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
